*Q1. What is UART?**  
UART is a hardware communication protocol used to transmit and receive serial data between devices.

**Q2. Why use a circular buffer for UART?**  
It efficiently uses memory and allows continuous data transfer without shifting existing data.

**Q3. What happens when the buffer is full?**  
New data may be lost due to overflow unless the buffer is managed properly.

**Q4. Is UART synchronous or asynchronous?**  
UART is asynchronous because it does not use a separate clock signal for synchronization.

**Q5. What is baud rate?**  
Baud rate is the number of signal symbols transmitted per second; in typical UART, it corresponds numerically to bits per se
